{"t": 1795069446.584306, "kind": "assistant", "text": "## PHP 8.3 upgrade report\n\n- **Inventory:** Dev and prod were both running WordPress 6.9 on PHP 8.1.34.\n- **Snapshot:** Dev files and database were saved as `dev/pre-php-8.3-upgrade.tgz`.\n- **Dev upgrade:** PHP upgraded successfully to **8.3.31**.\n- **Validation failed:** Both `/` and `/?p=1` returned **HTTP 500 — PHP fatal error**. The error names the active security plugin **`limit-login-attempts-reloaded` v3.4.4**.\n- **Action stopped:** I did not deactivate or modify the plugin and made no further changes. This compatibility issue must be investigated before any production upgrade.\n- **Production:** Untouched and still on PHP 8.1.34. No production change plan was submitted because dev validation failed.\n\nI could not read the contact-form comments: the available checker exposes only status codes/error categories, not comment content. The comments page also now returns HTTP 500."}
